# 17. WHY SERVICES MATTER

Imagine:

```text
Windows Service
      ↓
Runs as SYSTEM
      ↓
Executes program
      ↓
Program is writable by normal user
```

This can create a privilege-escalation path.

Conceptually:

```text
Low Privileged User
        ↓
Modify privileged executable
        ↓
SYSTEM service executes it
        ↓
Potential privilege escalation
```

---

# 18. SERVICE ACCOUNT

A service may run as:

- Local System
- Local Service
- Network Service
- Dedicated service account

Check the service configuration carefully.

Example:

```cmd
sc qc <service>
```

---

# 19. WEAK SERVICE PERMISSIONS

Suppose a normal user can modify:

- Service executable
- Service configuration
- Service-related directory

while the service runs with SYSTEM privileges.

This may be a serious escalation path.

The important question is:

> **Can the low-privileged user influence what the privileged service executes?**

