# 21. UNQUOTED SERVICE PATH

A classic Windows security issue is an improperly quoted executable path containing spaces.

Example:

```text id="vcs0pk"
C:\Program Files\Example App\service.exe
```

If the service path is improperly configured, Windows command-line parsing can potentially produce unexpected executable resolution.

Important:

> An unquoted service path is a **potential vulnerability**, not automatic privilege escalation.

---

# 22. SAFE EXAM CONCEPT

Remember:

```text
SYSTEM service
      ↓
Unquoted path with spaces
      ↓
Unexpected executable resolution
      ↓
Potential escalation
```

The actual exploitability depends on:

- Directory permissions
- Existing files
- Service configuration
- Execution context

